From 631a6d6c20a6c6217a79aaf5b933adbd87b1c252 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: austin62jake <340374338+austin62jake@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 04:31:39 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] fix(motion): a plain two-ring bar fits its true axis and
 wraps; the seam refusal names its causes

A bar meshed as two rings (long side facets, axis-fan caps - how CAD
exports a cylinder) was refused by the rotary wrap as "a feature that
is not turned crosses the seam". The cause was the axis fit: every side
facet anchors its normal line at the bar's mid-station, so no line sees
a tilt about it. The eigen direction was exact, but the refinement
returned a 26-microradian tilt and the fit kept it on a residual lower
by rounding noise. The leaning axis put the cap centres a micron off it
at arbitrary azimuths, and their facets read as 15 to 38 seam columns.

- axis_refine::worth_refining: an eigen line already concurrent to
  rounding (residual under 1e-9 mm per mm of radius) is not refined.
- rotary_seam: seam columns are grouped at the weld grid's grain
  (1e-6 rad, was 1e-9), still far finer than any flat's ragged seam.
- The seam refusal also names a mesh whose diameters were tessellated
  with different column counts, and says what to do about each cause.

Fixes #228

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
